From 0971cd9debc2438e61df7167551d276a210776fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 21:16:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): bf16x2 epilogue and next-tile key prefetch in
 the dense indexer score kernel

Base: candidate-60 vLLM patch head f27a89d6a94470857bc70bce580e84b7efe2b696 (tree afcaac3594ac).

Rationale:
At long prefill the dense indexer of layers 2, 8 and 14 is almost all of the cost that grows
with context: on candidate-60 at tp4-ring the time per prompt token rises from 100.9 us at
122K tokens to 110.3 us at 910K, and a 256-row sub-chunk's score and top-512 account for
9.2 of those 9.4 us, the score kernel for 80% of it. In __tl_score_rows_dense_fast:
1. The epilogue computes bf16(max(bf16(dot), 0) * w) with __hmax2 and __hmul2 on bf16x2 pairs
   instead of a round trip through float2 (cvt, fmaxf, fmul, cvt). The product of two BF16
   values is exact in FP32, so the one bf16x2 rounding equals the float path's rounding of the
   exact product; __hmax2 returns the non-NaN operand as fmaxf does.
2. The head sum reads two heads per 32-bit shared-memory load: the swizzle mask is even, so
   heads 2k and 2k + 1 stay adjacent, and they are added low then high, the same FP32 additions
   in increasing head order.
3. On the fast path (rows sharing row 0's pages), the next tile's key and scale reads are
   issued as soon as the current tile is in registers and stored to shared memory at the next
   iteration (__tl_fetch_k_dense / __tl_store_k_shared: the loader's addresses and predicates,
   one tile ahead). Any other path ignores the prefetched words.

Quality:
Bit-identical: every score over every row's extent and every selected position, against the
candidate-60 kernel at prefill depths of 122K, 237K, 470K and 910K-token prompts (256-row
sub-chunks, ratio-2 cache) and at the decode shapes of benchmark_deepseek_v41_indexer_bound.py
(6 and 96 rows, 4K to 1M keys). Score kernel 19-22% faster at prefill depths (about 209 against
160 TFLOPS on GB10); no decode case slower. End to end at tp4-ring (same image, same prompts,
2 boots each): cold prefill +0.5% at 122K, +1.2% at 237K, +1.0% at 470K and +2.1% at 910K
tokens (9,064 -> 9,251 tok/s).

Tests:
- pytest tests/kernels/attention/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang.py -k "indexer or topk" (28 passed,
  1 skipped, 1 xfailed: the non-finite query-scale contract, unchanged here).
- pytest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v41_tilelang_pdl.py (15 passed).

Upstream status: local DeepSeek-V4.1 TileLang indexer optimization for SM120/SM121.
